<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sri Vikrama Rajasinha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1780–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sri Vikrama Rajasinha was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, reigning from 1798 to 1815, of the South Indian Nayak dynasty. His harsh rule alienated the Kandyan nobility, who conspired with the British. A British force entered Kandy in 1815, he was deposed under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention">Kandyan Convention</a> and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vellore">Vellore</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sri-vikrama-rajasinha.jpg" alt="Sri Vikrama Rajasinha" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vikrama_Rajasinha_Kandy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
